id: pm-github-hptv
title: Bound native Bun CLI repeats of a completed public atomic import
description: "The final packed candidate imported three public issues and passed its Node repeat, privacy gate, and strict health. A direct native Bun CLI repeat remained active with substantial CPU use and was terminated after a bounded acceptance run; tracker bytes stayed unchanged. Earlier native Bun acceptance and library harness tests passed, so the installed-host boundary needs a minimal synthetic reproduction before assigning an upstream cause. Keep this separate from passing Node workflow safety and from the all-source coverage blocker."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T08:28:54.625Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T09:55:33.050Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T09:07:19.298Z",codex-sol,"A fresh bounded native Bun CLI repeat of the latest packed candidate passed in 4.22 seconds with exit zero and byte-identical tracker contents. This contrasts with the earlier long-running repeat, so retain the issue as an intermittent installed-host investigation rather than claiming a consistent Bun failure. All 375 native Bun library and operational tests also pass."
  "2026-10-05T09:55:33.050Z",codex-sol,"The final packed candidate matched all three authored runtime modules byte-for-byte. Its fresh Node public import passed with three issues, a byte-identical second run, zero gate findings, and strict health in 24.94 seconds. A bounded direct native Bun CLI repeat, using the same pinned host and startup executable path, timed out at 45.06 seconds and was terminated with SIGTERM; durable tracker bytes stayed unchanged. This reproduces the intermittent installed-host boundary alongside all 420 passing native Bun library and operational tests. No scratch remote was configured and no public-data push occurred."
